' Source: apps/api-node/src/modules/claims/application/claim.use-cases.ts
' Main entity migration: apps/api-node/src/migrations/002_lost_found_schema.sql
' One-table abstraction: related repository reads/writes stay inside the service.
actor "Claimant / Finder" as Actor
participant "Private Claims Page" as Page
participant "Claims API" as API
participant "Claim Service" as Service
participant "claims" as Table <<entity>>

Actor -> Page: 1: Open Create a claim request
activate Page
Page -> API: 2: POST /api/claims
activate API
API -> API: 3: Validate access session, role and input
alt Valid request
API -> Service: 4: Create a claim request
activate Service
Service -> Service: 5: Begin transaction; resolve active target or valid LOST/FOUND pair
Service -> Service: 6: Resolve actual owner/Finder; disallow self-contact and duplicates
Service -> Service: 7: For direct non-owner LOST contact: require fresh approved photo
alt Authorized source and communication gate satisfied
Service -> Table: 8: INSERT claim with request fingerprint
activate Table
Table --> Service: 9: Created claim
deactivate Table
Service -> Service: 10: Assign actual participant roles and consent; open direct room
Service -> Service: 11: Consume checked photo; attach protected IMAGE and PHOTO evidence
Service -> Service: 12: Write claim audit and notifications; commit
Service -> Service: 13: Return room without sending typed draft or verifying ownership
Service --> API: 14: Claim and authorized room
API --> Page: 15: HTTP 201 (200 on replay): Claim and authorized room
Page --> Actor: 16: Show authorized result
else Pair unavailable or required photo not approved
Service --> API: 8.1: Claim creation blocked
API --> Page: 8.2: HTTP 409
Page --> Actor: 8.3: Display error; do not report success
end
deactivate Service
else Invalid input, missing session or insufficient role
API --> Page: 4.1: HTTP 422 / 401 / 403 (429 only if rate-limited)
Page --> Actor: 4.2: Show appropriate error; retain form/draft
end
deactivate API
deactivate Page

legend left
Scope: Direct LOST contact requires similarity >=50% AND analysis confidence >=60%. FOUND
publication is not required. Matched requests may start PENDING; creation never approves ownership.
endlegend
